I'm happy to announce the first experimental online feature of Web Host Simulator: the website ServerOverflow.whs, where players can share knowledge and troubleshoot issues. Each accepted answer earns the player 10 points, which are added to the points received from other users, contributing to their overall score on the Top Users leaderboard. This system encourages active participation and rewards helpfulness within the community.

[b]Changelog[/b]
[list]
[*] Added the website ServerOverflow.whs;
[*] Added an enterable quantity field in the ShopIT cart;
[*] Reworked the website loading logic in the FlyBird browser, significantly reducing the UI construction recalculation time when loading pages;
[*] Fixed a bug where a removed HDD would not be unlinked from the equipment;
[*] Resolved an issue where the "clear" command rendered FlockCMD and SwitchCMD unusable;
[*] Corrected a display bug where 16GB RAM was shown as 8GB on the assembly table;
[*] Fixed a bug where the server room reflection probe was not updated when the quality setting was low or medium;
[*] Addressed an issue where the correct and incorrect icon was not displayed when installing a cable in the rear ports of the Patch Panel.
[/list]
I don't usually include things done outside the game in the changelog, but I would like to add that a moderation panel was also created so that moderators can oversee player-generated content on ServerOverflow. Additionally, an [url=https://store.steampowered.com/eula/1318990_eula_0]End User License Agreement (EULA)[/url] and a [url=https://webhostsimulator.com/privacy]Privacy Policy[/url] were created to help us expand our online features soon.

